^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-04-04 11:24] observe — the current hook performs staged file collection, check execution, report rendering, and Touch ID authorization in one shell surface.
 >>[2026-04-04 11:24] observe — poll-review and the hook overlap semantically but do not yet read like two surfaces of one shared review engine.
 >>[2026-04-04 11:25] decide — redesign around informed authorization: checks first, summary second, authorization last.
 >>[2026-04-04 11:25] decide — plan a shared review runner plus narrower renderer and authorization boundary so the hook becomes orchestration instead of policy ballast.
 >>[2026-04-04 11:25] taste — the highest-value improvement is making the human authorize a concrete commit summary, not just a generic biometric prompt.
 >>[2026-04-04 11:47] observe — the versioned hook sources live under `scripts/`, while `.git/hooks/` is only the installed runtime copy; commit-worthy changes should land in the versioned scripts first.
 >>[2026-04-04 11:52] implement — extracted shared shell helpers for agent detection, staged review execution, and commit-message validation under `scripts/commit-review/`.
 >>[2026-04-04 11:53] implement — rewired `scripts/pre-commit` and `scripts/commit-msg` to delegate to the new shared helpers instead of owning the logic inline.
 >>[2026-04-04 11:54] verify — `bash -n scripts/pre-commit scripts/commit-msg scripts/commit-review/run-review.sh scripts/commit-review/validate-commit-message.sh scripts/commit-review/lib/agent-context.sh` passed.
 >>[2026-04-04 11:55] verify — `scripts/commit-review/run-review.sh` and `scripts/commit-msg` sample good/bad message checks behaved as expected.
 >>[2026-04-04 12:03] implement — added `render-review.sh` and `authorize-commit.sh` so summary rendering and authorization become separate commit-review surfaces.
 >>[2026-04-04 12:04] implement — updated `scripts/pre-commit` to render file-category summary + diffstat before auth and to block immediately on review errors.
 >>[2026-04-04 12:05] verify — `bash -n` passed for the new renderer/authorizer, and sourced `spw_commit_review_run` + `spw_render_commit_review` rendered the empty staged-state summary without auth side effects.
 >>[2026-04-04 12:10] implement — added local-context provenance resolution with heuristic fallback and surfaced actor/source/confidence in both commit-gate and poll-review outputs.
 >>[2026-04-04 12:12] implement — added explicit `set-agent-context.sh` and `clear-agent-context.sh` helpers so wrappers and humans can author provenance directly instead of relying on env guesses.
 >>[2026-04-04 12:13] verify — shell parse checks passed for the new context helpers; in this sandbox the writer cannot persist hidden-path state, but resolver output stays clean and falls back to heuristic provenance as designed.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:27] revise — Resolved ?[agent_source]: c4be2f46 added set-agent-context.sh and clear-agent-context.sh with a TTL-bound context file and a heuristic fallback, so SPW_AGENT alone is no longer the only source.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:27] revise — Commits 1 to 4 reconciled to five landed hashes in done; commit 5 (docs) remains because the workflow doc still covers only the Touch ID prompt. Two open questions sharpened.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:37] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 5 landed, 1 planned, 0 dropped.
 >>[2026-10-27 10:19] note — Linked .spw/caches/tree/spw/history/commit-gate.spw as a root: it walks the gate states read at 1aa1dc23 and records three gaps that still hold at 850077ab and that document_ceremony should state, not paper over. Under set -e a Touch ID helper exit of 2 ends the hook before the documented y/N fallback, so the gate fails closed; run-review.sh lists only added, copied, and modified files, so a commit of only deletions or renames, a rename with edits included, never prompts; and no tracked script installs scripts/pre-commit or scripts/commit-msg beyond the comment at scripts/pre-commit line 12. Roots, hot files, and the PLAN.md Files list now name scripts/pre-commit, the versioned hook, per the 2026-04-04 11:47 observation. Declared shares with tooling-scripts-consolidation, whose gate_dead_checks edits run-review.sh and poll-review.sh.
 >>[2026-10-27 13:01] note — plan-tooling-design landing_from_episodes (2026-10-27) would have each commit episode name the plan labels it lands, and asks in ?[lands_syntax] whether the commit-msg hook refuses a label no plan holds; the episode format stays this plan to keep.
}

^["open"]{
